1
00:00:14,120 --> 00:00:18,420
Aiming for the setting sun
floating over the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:18,420 --> 00:00:23,900
I kick a pebble and fly off with the bear,

3
00:00:24,480 --> 00:00:29,360
to Kashiwa,
the type who was always joking around,

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,800
they laughed that I'm still just a kid.

5
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:36,140
Somewhere, a little good energy,

6
00:00:36,140 --> 00:00:38,680
even as a sound,
only the serious ones are solid.

7
00:00:38,680 --> 00:00:41,940
One bad habit, the unchanging streetscape,

8
00:00:41,940 --> 00:00:43,880
is kinder.

9
00:00:44,620 --> 00:00:46,860
Because the crows are crying,

10
00:00:46,860 --> 00:00:48,960
the day is already ending, isn't it?

11
00:00:49,640 --> 00:00:53,840
Are the yakitori really there?

12
00:00:54,800 --> 00:00:57,460
Of the pointy hat,

13
00:00:57,460 --> 00:01:02,440
from the canal to the giant fireworks,

14
00:01:02,440 --> 00:01:04,060
the sunset falls.

15
00:01:06,720 --> 00:01:10,080
Tomorrow too,
it'll end just like this, won't it?

16
00:01:10,080 --> 00:01:12,720
We're just mongrels laughing,
and happiness too.

17
00:01:12,720 --> 00:01:14,640
Taking it easy, I realized,

18
00:01:14,640 --> 00:01:16,300
because I'm a fool.

19
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:17,600
Yeah

20
00:01:25,220 --> 00:01:27,240
Intense Run:
The Narrow Road to the Deep North

21
00:01:39,180 --> 00:01:40,460
N-Nana-chan

22
00:01:41,760 --> 00:01:44,000
Honda doesn't understand

23
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:46,600
how hard I have it.

24
00:01:47,600 --> 00:01:49,140
I hate Honda.

25
00:01:50,420 --> 00:01:51,340
Nana-chan

26
00:01:54,340 --> 00:01:58,240
The customer you are
calling is out of range,

27
00:01:58,640 --> 00:01:59,680
Nana-chan

28
00:02:03,400 --> 00:02:04,500
An old pond,

29
00:02:05,180 --> 00:02:07,620
a frog jumps in, the sound of water.

30
00:02:07,620 --> 00:02:10,040
What are you talking about?

31
00:02:10,380 --> 00:02:13,000
A grown-up like you doesn't
even know Matsuo Bashō?

32
00:02:13,240 --> 00:02:14,260
Matsuo Bashō?

33
00:02:14,260 --> 00:02:18,900
Yeah, the haiku master from the Edo period.
Look, right over there.

34
00:02:20,740 --> 00:02:22,940
So this is Bashō.

35
00:02:24,040 --> 00:02:28,460
Matsuo Bashō set out on his Narrow Road to
the Deep North journey from here in Fukagawa.

36
00:02:29,180 --> 00:02:30,260
The Narrow Road to the Deep North?

37
00:02:30,260 --> 00:02:35,920
Yeah, only by traveling the Narrow Road
do you understand the essence of life.

38
00:02:36,440 --> 00:02:40,880
The essence of life You're
thinking deep thoughts.

39
00:02:43,200 --> 00:02:46,400
Actually, this is something my grandpa says.

40
00:02:46,400 --> 00:02:49,440
My grandpa really loves Bashō.

41
00:02:49,440 --> 00:02:51,880
So you were influenced by that

42
00:02:52,680 --> 00:02:54,000
I'm Matsuo Kyūichi.

43
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:55,680
I'm Hayato Honda.

44
00:02:55,680 --> 00:02:59,040
Hey, why were you crying just now?

45
00:03:00,620 --> 00:03:03,020
Looks like you caught me
in an embarrassing moment.

46
00:03:03,720 --> 00:03:05,740
Did you get into a fight
with a friend or something?

47
00:03:06,640 --> 00:03:07,880
It's my fault.

48
00:03:09,380 --> 00:03:12,360
Is the climax draft really okay like this?

49
00:03:12,440 --> 00:03:14,540
Should I change it after all?

50
00:03:14,940 --> 00:03:19,140
She was troubled about her work,
so I thought I'd try to cheer her up.

51
00:03:21,120 --> 00:03:21,660
Well,

52
00:03:21,660 --> 00:03:27,240
I got to read the manuscript for that manga too,
and it was really interesting.

53
00:03:27,620 --> 00:03:30,780
Maybe people who've been fans for a long time
will be a little surprised, though.

54
00:03:31,340 --> 00:03:32,120
Honda-san...

55
00:03:33,620 --> 00:03:37,740
I know how hard you worked to finish it,
Nana-chan,

56
00:03:37,740 --> 00:03:39,540
so I want you to have confidence in it.

57
00:03:40,120 --> 00:03:41,800
Honda-san, be quiet.

58
00:03:43,120 --> 00:03:44,340
Nana-chan...

59
00:03:44,340 --> 00:03:46,780
Honda-san, you couldn't possibly understand
how I feel.

60
00:03:47,260 --> 00:03:49,480
You don't know anything about my struggles.

61
00:03:50,840 --> 00:03:51,840
Nana-chan...

62
00:03:52,780 --> 00:03:56,560
I just wanted to be of some help to you, Nana-chan,
even a little.

63
00:03:56,560 --> 00:04:00,280
But now that I think about it,
my advice is probably just a nuisance

64
00:04:02,900 --> 00:04:04,660
I don't think it's that bad.

65
00:04:05,980 --> 00:04:08,440
I think so, but somehow...

66
00:04:09,920 --> 00:04:10,320
Thanks.

67
00:04:11,900 --> 00:04:14,880
Stillness...
the cicadas' cries
sinking into the rocks.

68
00:04:14,880 --> 00:04:16,040
That's Bashō too.

69
00:04:16,040 --> 00:04:16,660
Yeah.

70
00:04:16,660 --> 00:04:18,920
Frogs and cicadas are interesting,
aren't they?

71
00:04:19,400 --> 00:04:21,980
Bashō was even called the poet of the ears.

72
00:04:21,980 --> 00:04:23,980
Many of his haiku were about sounds.

73
00:04:25,680 --> 00:04:29,340
Stillness...
the cicadas' cries
sinking into the rocks.

74
00:04:30,820 --> 00:04:32,180
Haiku are amazing, aren't they?

75
00:04:32,700 --> 00:04:34,960
They whisk you off to
another world in an instant.

76
00:04:35,960 --> 00:04:36,860
Haiku

77
00:04:37,280 --> 00:04:38,700
Stop moping around

78
00:04:38,700 --> 00:04:40,640
and make up with your friend.

79
00:04:41,260 --> 00:04:42,380
I've got to go now.

80
00:04:42,380 --> 00:04:42,820
Well, then.

81
00:04:44,720 --> 00:04:45,840
Thanks, see you.

82
00:04:46,980 --> 00:04:47,740
See you.

83
00:04:48,640 --> 00:04:49,440
Mm.

84
00:04:51,780 --> 00:04:53,660
Wh-whoa, the statue moved!

85
00:04:53,660 --> 00:04:54,720
Ha

86
00:04:54,720 --> 00:04:57,140
It moves at five in the evening.

87
00:04:57,140 --> 00:05:00,180
What?! W-why does the statue move?!

88
00:05:00,840 --> 00:05:06,300
Maybe it wants to show Bashō the different directions of the Sumida River,
the one he followed when he set off on the Narrow Road to the Deep North.

89
00:05:09,180 --> 00:05:14,440
Even after he died, to be treated like that...
Bashō really was an amazing man.

90
00:05:16,980 --> 00:05:22,060
Nana-chan, sorry about today.
Good luck with your work. Honda

91
00:05:22,980 --> 00:05:23,740
Haah...

92
00:05:25,500 --> 00:05:30,020
The days and months are the
travelers of a hundred generations,

93
00:05:30,020 --> 00:05:31,920
Imitating a duck is the real thing.

94
00:05:31,920 --> 00:05:33,480
No, that's not it.

95
00:05:33,480 --> 00:05:35,700
It's Matsuo Bashō's Oku no Hosomichi.

96
00:05:35,700 --> 00:05:38,340
The days and months are the
travelers of a hundred generations,

97
00:05:38,340 --> 00:05:41,060
and the years that come
and go are travelers too.

98
00:05:41,460 --> 00:05:43,140
Those are the opening lines
of Oku no Hosomichi, right?

99
00:05:43,140 --> 00:05:44,580
As expected of you.

100
00:05:44,580 --> 00:05:45,760
What does it mean?

101
00:05:46,300 --> 00:05:48,540
The days and months are eternal travelers,

102
00:05:48,540 --> 00:05:51,240
and the years that come
and go are also travelers.

103
00:05:51,240 --> 00:05:52,720
That's what it means.

104
00:05:53,740 --> 00:05:55,040
The months and days are travelers.

105
00:05:55,700 --> 00:05:57,160
Even if you ask me why,

106
00:05:57,540 --> 00:05:59,940
Nakagawa can't explain it well either.

107
00:05:59,940 --> 00:06:02,620
Even Honda doesn't really know, does he?

108
00:06:02,620 --> 00:06:05,420
Because it's only been a short while,
you know.

109
00:06:05,420 --> 00:06:09,140
Honda, why did you suddenly
become interested in Bashō?

110
00:06:10,280 --> 00:06:13,140
I happened to meet an elementary
schooler who knows a lot about Bashō.

111
00:06:13,680 --> 00:06:15,780
What an elementary schooler
with such refined tastes.

112
00:06:16,140 --> 00:06:18,680
Apparently his grandfather
is a big fan of Bashō.

113
00:06:19,280 --> 00:06:20,080
I see.

114
00:06:20,080 --> 00:06:22,000
That's when I met him on
the banks of the Sumida River.

115
00:06:23,800 --> 00:06:26,540
This guy got dumped by Nana Otohime.

116
00:06:26,540 --> 00:06:30,300
No, we just had a slight
difference of opinion.

117
00:06:30,800 --> 00:06:33,280
But you haven't been able to reach Otohime since then,
have you?

118
00:06:33,280 --> 00:06:36,380
That's what people in
general call getting dumped.

119
00:06:36,880 --> 00:06:40,360
A top-selling manga artist and
you are worlds apart to begin with.

120
00:06:40,760 --> 00:06:43,020
You should give up and accept that it
was a love that was never meant to be.

121
00:06:43,020 --> 00:06:44,140
Oh no, oh no, oh no.

122
00:06:44,140 --> 00:06:48,620
Did that schoolboy really cheer
up Honda when he was feeling down?

123
00:06:49,200 --> 00:06:52,540
The Bashō haiku he read to
me really sank into my heart.

124
00:06:53,740 --> 00:06:57,800
I was so soothed by it.
That's why I bought this book.

125
00:06:57,800 --> 00:06:58,880
Is that right?

126
00:06:58,880 --> 00:07:00,060
What a nice story.

127
00:07:00,060 --> 00:07:05,840
Even I know that spot. It's the one where the
frog jumped into the pond and farted, right?

128
00:07:06,260 --> 00:07:07,640
Ryo-chan, you...

129
00:07:07,640 --> 00:07:09,160
That's totally wrong.

130
00:07:09,160 --> 00:07:11,380
So that's how it sounds to you, senpai.

131
00:07:11,380 --> 00:07:16,880
I could come up with funnier haiku all day long,
gushing out like a spring.

132
00:07:16,880 --> 00:07:21,220
I can sort of predict the haiku
that'll gush out of Ryo-san's spring.

133
00:07:21,220 --> 00:07:23,160
I don't think we even need to hear it.

134
00:07:23,740 --> 00:07:24,920
Honestly, I'd rather not hear it.

135
00:07:25,540 --> 00:07:28,100
You lot can just keep mocking me like that.

136
00:07:28,100 --> 00:07:30,500
That I have a writer's talent

137
00:07:30,860 --> 00:07:33,680
is obvious from my
track record of hit manga.

138
00:07:34,340 --> 00:07:36,020
Haiku's a cinch, you know.

139
00:07:36,020 --> 00:07:37,560
If you're that confident,

140
00:07:37,560 --> 00:07:39,780
why don't you enter this?

141
00:07:39,780 --> 00:07:40,180
Chief.

142
00:07:40,580 --> 00:07:41,760
Good morning.

143
00:07:41,760 --> 00:07:43,060
Morning.

144
00:07:43,060 --> 00:07:43,960
What is it?

145
00:07:44,660 --> 00:07:47,340
The Mainichi Shimbun haiku contest.

146
00:07:47,340 --> 00:07:49,800
That's a contest with a long history.

147
00:07:50,740 --> 00:07:54,000
First prize is 3 million yen.
Chief, I'm entering.

148
00:07:54,600 --> 00:07:56,560
Let's go for that 3 million!

149
00:07:56,560 --> 00:07:58,660
Jan-jan bari-bari, 585!

150
00:07:58,660 --> 00:08:01,320
Haiku is 575, Ryo-san.

151
00:08:01,320 --> 00:08:02,000
Done!

152
00:08:02,840 --> 00:08:06,420
Blew all my cash on
pachinko and got cleaned out.

153
00:08:06,420 --> 00:08:09,380
Quit pachinko and switched
over to the horse races.

154
00:08:09,380 --> 00:08:10,580
There's still more to come!

155
00:08:10,580 --> 00:08:13,180
Wordplay seems to be all you can manage

156
00:08:13,840 --> 00:08:17,080
A dark horse, and a miracle jackpot payout!

157
00:08:17,080 --> 00:08:18,720
Knock it off, Bakabon!

158
00:08:18,720 --> 00:08:24,940
Listen, haiku is written by working
a seasonal kigo into five-seven-five.

159
00:08:24,940 --> 00:08:30,380
Spring or summer, you fit a seasonal
image into seventeen syllables.

160
00:08:31,040 --> 00:08:35,300
You don't even know that, and you're aiming for first prize?
Laughable.

161
00:08:35,300 --> 00:08:39,400
I know, I know, just throw in a kigo,
that's all, right?

162
00:08:39,980 --> 00:08:45,720
Spring Try the Oga Prize or the Emperor's Cup,
how about a big payout?

163
00:08:46,720 --> 00:08:49,700
My chronic lower back pain
has been acting up again lately.

164
00:08:49,700 --> 00:08:51,780
That's bad.

165
00:08:51,780 --> 00:08:54,800
Hey! You can't just ignore me, Chief!

166
00:08:55,280 --> 00:08:56,520
Baka-bon!

167
00:08:56,520 --> 00:08:58,300
The Grand Prize or the Emperor's Cup,
you say?

168
00:08:58,380 --> 00:09:00,760
Then enter the Japan
Racing Association instead!

169
00:09:00,900 --> 00:09:04,340
I enter the Japan Racing Association every week,
with my losing betting tickets.

170
00:09:04,340 --> 00:09:05,960
Matsuo-kun!

171
00:09:06,380 --> 00:09:08,600
He's the elementary schoolboy
I met by the Sumida River.

172
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:13,860
In the elementary school division,
last year's champion, Kyūichi Matsuo,

173
00:09:15,740 --> 00:09:17,800
the leading expert in
researching the locations

174
00:09:18,200 --> 00:09:20,220
and is the grandson of Mr. Matsuo Bashō,

175
00:09:20,220 --> 00:09:23,580
a prodigy of the haiku world from
whom great things are expected.

176
00:09:23,580 --> 00:09:25,720
He didn't just get selected,
he won first place!

177
00:09:25,720 --> 00:09:29,040
I've seen this old man on TV too!

178
00:09:29,040 --> 00:09:30,900
Life is a journey.

179
00:09:31,340 --> 00:09:33,780
Only by making a journey along
the Narrow Road to the Deep North

180
00:09:33,780 --> 00:09:36,400
can you understand what life truly is.

181
00:09:36,400 --> 00:09:38,800
I want to say this to you young people too.

182
00:09:38,800 --> 00:09:41,180
Instead of playing games
at home all the time,

183
00:09:41,180 --> 00:09:44,420
go and take a journey along the
Narrow Road to the Deep North once.

184
00:09:45,720 --> 00:09:50,200
Oh yes, that program actually just
featured the Narrow Road to the Deep North.

185
00:09:50,200 --> 00:09:57,060
Matsuo-kun is a famous person's grandson? The grandson of last year's winner,
the board director.

186
00:09:58,100 --> 00:10:01,300
The haiku prodigy is Honda's acquaintance.

187
00:10:03,320 --> 00:10:04,720
We could get 3 million yen!

188
00:10:10,660 --> 00:10:11,640
Here it is, sir.

189
00:10:11,640 --> 00:10:13,700
Go through this gate and climb the stairs,

190
00:10:13,700 --> 00:10:15,380
and there's a Bashō statue.

191
00:10:16,320 --> 00:10:18,980
The shrine nearby has Bashō's new

192
00:10:19,860 --> 00:10:22,020
You really know your way around here now.

193
00:10:22,020 --> 00:10:25,580
Climb those stairs and over
there is the Sumida River.

194
00:10:28,780 --> 00:10:31,240
I met him around there the other day.

195
00:10:31,240 --> 00:10:34,860
I'd really love to get some
haiku pointers from a master.

196
00:10:34,860 --> 00:10:39,520
And if his distinguished grandfather puts in a word for me,
the 3-million-yen first prize.

197
00:10:39,520 --> 00:10:40,260
Here he comes.

198
00:10:40,780 --> 00:10:41,680
That's him.

199
00:10:44,540 --> 00:10:45,740
He's crying.

200
00:10:45,740 --> 00:10:47,260
Young Master Matsuo.

201
00:10:47,960 --> 00:10:48,360
Who?

202
00:10:50,080 --> 00:10:53,400
Actually,
I was hoping you'd look at a haiku I wrote.

203
00:10:54,940 --> 00:10:58,680
Sorry for the sudden,
unreasonable request, Matsuo-kun.

204
00:10:58,680 --> 00:10:59,900
Yeah, sure.

205
00:11:04,320 --> 00:11:06,240
I did keep the setting in mind, at least.

206
00:11:06,660 --> 00:11:10,140
A bush warbler: ho-ho-hokekyo, ho-ho-hoke.

207
00:11:10,140 --> 00:11:12,740
You should give up on winning a prize.
It's impossible.

208
00:11:12,740 --> 00:11:13,320
Just as I thought.

209
00:11:13,320 --> 00:11:15,920
Even a seasonal word like
that is in there, see?

210
00:11:16,900 --> 00:11:20,760
Tree frog, gero gero gegero gero gero gēro

211
00:11:20,760 --> 00:11:22,300
That's a bit of a rip-off, isn't it?

212
00:11:23,440 --> 00:11:24,940
Well, entering is free, I suppose.

213
00:11:25,980 --> 00:11:27,620
Damn this cocky little brat!

214
00:11:27,620 --> 00:11:29,640
But if I upset him here,

215
00:11:31,240 --> 00:11:34,380
it's all for nothing. I'll just
grit my teeth for the three million.

216
00:11:35,120 --> 00:11:38,680
Then would you introduce
me to your grandfather?

217
00:11:39,100 --> 00:11:42,140
I'll do anything in return,
so please, just this once.

218
00:11:42,140 --> 00:11:43,780
Please, please.

219
00:11:43,780 --> 00:11:45,100
That's unreasonable, senpai.

220
00:11:47,140 --> 00:11:49,020
I have a place I want to go, though.

221
00:11:49,020 --> 00:11:52,500
If you take me there,
I'll introduce you to my grandpa.

222
00:11:53,060 --> 00:11:54,240
Alright, let's go!

223
00:11:54,520 --> 00:11:56,906
Where? Odaiba, or Roppongi,

224
00:11:56,956 --> 00:11:59,740
Shiodome, or the amusement park in Chiba?

225
00:12:01,240 --> 00:12:05,760
The place I want to go is the Narrow Road to the Deep North,
the 2,400 km Bashō walked.

226
00:12:05,760 --> 00:12:15,000
2,400 km? What an eccentric little brat with old-fashioned tastes you are!
No problem, Honda, I'll take him.

227
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:25,080
Boy: But will my family even let me go?
Ryotsu: No need to worry about that. Your grandpa's been promoting my Narrow Road, after all.

228
00:12:25,080 --> 00:12:27,280
Are you taking me or not?

229
00:12:27,480 --> 00:12:31,600
But a 2,400 km trip with a
kid is a huge journey, senpai.

230
00:12:31,600 --> 00:12:35,400
He's just a kid. Will he notice
if we skip a bit of the route?

231
00:12:35,400 --> 00:12:38,880
Just ride a motorbike around
the Kanto area in a loop.

232
00:12:38,880 --> 00:12:40,780
Use your head a little.

233
00:12:44,640 --> 00:12:47,940
Matsuo-kun really needs this trip right now,
doesn't he.

234
00:12:48,540 --> 00:12:52,280
Alright, let's travel the Narrow Road together,
Matsuo-kun.

235
00:12:52,280 --> 00:12:53,140
Yes!

236
00:12:55,720 --> 00:12:59,480
That's great, Matsuo-kun.
Your mom and dad gave you permission.

237
00:12:59,480 --> 00:13:03,560
Great, great. Now you can get us
introduced to your grandfather.

238
00:13:03,560 --> 00:13:06,340
Yeah, I'll introduce you when we get back.

239
00:13:06,340 --> 00:13:09,120
Then I'll come pick you
up early tomorrow morning.

240
00:13:09,120 --> 00:13:09,560
OK.

241
00:13:10,440 --> 00:13:11,540
Mr. Ryusenshi.

242
00:13:11,540 --> 00:13:12,520
Yoshiko.

243
00:13:12,520 --> 00:13:15,060
I've finished the manuscript,
so I came to deliver it.

244
00:13:15,880 --> 00:13:18,500
If you'd just called,
I would have come to pick it up.

245
00:13:18,500 --> 00:13:22,100
I have something I need to apologize to you for,
Mr. Ryusenshi.

246
00:13:33,260 --> 00:13:35,520
So, Miko,
you want to keep going like this, then?

247
00:13:36,460 --> 00:13:38,320
Yes, I'm sorry for being selfish.

248
00:13:38,760 --> 00:13:41,680
Why are you apologizing?
I'm happy about it, Miko.

249
00:13:43,380 --> 00:13:46,020
In a way,
this is an adventure for the Love Miko.

250
00:13:46,520 --> 00:13:49,180
Some fans might leave us.

251
00:13:50,320 --> 00:13:52,020
It was really interesting.

252
00:13:52,020 --> 00:13:56,100
Fans who've been with you all along
might be a little surprised, though.

253
00:13:56,100 --> 00:13:56,460
For you

254
00:13:56,460 --> 00:14:01,320
If you have that resolve,
I'll gladly fight alongside you.

255
00:14:01,820 --> 00:14:02,940
Dragon Warrior-san

256
00:14:04,040 --> 00:14:05,460
Let's go with this one this time.

257
00:14:06,060 --> 00:14:06,460
Thank you very much.

258
00:14:08,080 --> 00:14:08,480
Thanks.

259
00:14:09,080 --> 00:14:09,960
Honda-san

260
00:14:09,960 --> 00:14:12,640
How do you feel, Matsuo, my boy?

261
00:14:12,640 --> 00:14:13,900
Yeah, I feel great.

262
00:14:14,700 --> 00:14:16,940
You seem somehow different
from your usual Honda-kun.

263
00:14:20,980 --> 00:14:24,440
I wonder where Honda-san
and Matsuo-kun are about now.

264
00:14:24,440 --> 00:14:27,240
Probably somewhere around
the cedar avenue at Imaichi.

265
00:14:27,240 --> 00:14:31,560
Okay, it's done. When they get back, I'll
learn the secret to winning the three million.

266
00:14:31,940 --> 00:14:33,460
If I do say so myself, it's a good one.

267
00:14:34,260 --> 00:14:36,100
Is there a police officer named Honda here?

268
00:14:38,440 --> 00:14:40,000
The haiku class teacher.

269
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:40,580
What?

270
00:14:41,400 --> 00:14:43,480
Then, Matsuo-kun's grandfather.

271
00:14:44,140 --> 00:14:44,927
Mr. Matsuo,

272
00:14:44,977 --> 00:14:48,160
I've actually been dabbling
in haiku for many years myself,

273
00:14:49,240 --> 00:14:51,860
and I was planning to enter the
Mainichi Shimbun haiku contest.

274
00:14:51,860 --> 00:14:54,420
I've been writing haiku like this.

275
00:14:55,680 --> 00:14:59,200
I heard that my grandson Kyūichi had gone
off with a police officer named Honda,

276
00:14:59,200 --> 00:15:00,640
I heard it from someone at home.

277
00:15:00,640 --> 00:15:04,500
The two set out early this morning on a
journey along the Narrow Road to the Deep North.

278
00:15:04,500 --> 00:15:06,640
What? The Narrow Road to the Deep North?

279
00:15:06,760 --> 00:15:09,520
Kyūichi's parents should
know about this, though.

280
00:15:09,520 --> 00:15:10,980
I haven't heard anything about it.

281
00:15:10,980 --> 00:15:12,800
Call them back right away.

282
00:15:14,460 --> 00:15:17,600
Your grandson was really
looking forward to this trip.

283
00:15:18,020 --> 00:15:19,800
First of all, he's still just a child.

284
00:15:19,800 --> 00:15:21,440
What if he gets hurt?

285
00:15:21,440 --> 00:15:23,140
Call him back right away.

286
00:15:23,140 --> 00:15:24,620
Yes, I'll call him back immediately.

287
00:15:25,280 --> 00:15:26,400
Who the hell is that?

288
00:15:26,400 --> 00:15:29,480
Kankichi Ryotsu is a
man who lives for haiku.

289
00:15:29,840 --> 00:15:32,260
Beep-boop-bop, I'll page him right now.

290
00:15:33,240 --> 00:15:35,120
If we upset the grandfather,
the one who matters most,

291
00:15:35,120 --> 00:15:36,740
we'll lose everything,
including the three million yen.

292
00:15:36,740 --> 00:15:40,640
Is the customer's phone
somewhere out of signal range?

293
00:15:40,640 --> 00:15:42,240
At least set it to voicemail.

294
00:15:43,480 --> 00:15:44,580
What's wrong, can't we get in touch?

295
00:15:44,580 --> 00:15:45,780
I'm back.

296
00:15:45,780 --> 00:15:47,100
I'll make some tea.

297
00:15:47,100 --> 00:15:48,580
I'll go buy some sweets to go with the tea.

298
00:15:49,200 --> 00:15:50,780
I'm going out on patrol.

299
00:15:50,780 --> 00:15:52,400
You lot.

300
00:15:53,520 --> 00:15:55,100
If anything happens to my grandson,

301
00:15:55,100 --> 00:15:56,280
you won't get off lightly.

302
00:15:56,280 --> 00:15:57,580
Understood.

303
00:15:57,580 --> 00:15:59,340
We'll go find him right away.

304
00:16:01,120 --> 00:16:02,380
I'm sorry.

305
00:16:03,180 --> 00:16:04,960
I have to catch a woman quickly.

306
00:16:05,320 --> 00:16:06,960
The 3 million yen is going to slip away!

307
00:16:07,940 --> 00:16:11,220
Ara tōtō, aoba wakaba no hi no hikari.

308
00:16:13,480 --> 00:16:15,000
Honda-kun, that's Nikkō over there.

309
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:16,580
What a magnificent view.

310
00:16:19,880 --> 00:16:22,340
Alright, shall we take a break around here?

311
00:16:22,340 --> 00:16:22,820
Yeah.

312
00:16:28,340 --> 00:16:30,560
Yay, kelp onigiri!

313
00:16:31,580 --> 00:16:34,540
Honda, you're a different person from
when you're riding that auto-bike.

314
00:16:34,540 --> 00:16:35,900
Yeah, I hear that a lot.

315
00:16:36,360 --> 00:16:37,980
Matsuo, yours is plum.

316
00:16:37,980 --> 00:16:38,401
Yeah.

317
00:16:38,451 --> 00:16:42,380
Matsuo, do you dislike plum?
Want me to swap it for yours?

318
00:16:45,820 --> 00:16:46,140
I'm fine.

319
00:16:46,600 --> 00:16:49,100
Man, I'm glad we came, Matsuo.

320
00:16:49,100 --> 00:16:51,640
Grandpa always says it on TV.

321
00:16:51,640 --> 00:16:55,320
that you only understand the true meaning
of life by traveling the Narrow Road.

322
00:16:55,700 --> 00:16:58,080
Matsuo,
you're really amazing for someone so young.

323
00:16:58,080 --> 00:16:59,780
I'm not amazing or anything.

324
00:16:59,780 --> 00:17:02,080
You look up to your grandpa, don't you?

325
00:17:02,080 --> 00:17:03,080
You love him

326
00:17:04,060 --> 00:17:05,400
I hate him. Grandpa's the worst.

327
00:17:07,200 --> 00:17:08,580
Your grandpa...

328
00:17:08,580 --> 00:17:11,940
On TV, everyone's saying you
should go on the Narrow Road, right?

329
00:17:12,400 --> 00:17:12,720
Yeah.

330
00:17:13,480 --> 00:17:15,080
So you've been there before, right?

331
00:17:16,320 --> 00:17:17,040
No, I haven't.

332
00:17:17,040 --> 00:17:20,620
So your grandpa's a liar!

333
00:17:20,620 --> 00:17:21,360
Liar!

334
00:17:22,580 --> 00:17:24,120
He's not a liar.

335
00:17:25,020 --> 00:17:27,860
The Narrow Road is too early for you.

336
00:17:28,620 --> 00:17:30,340
But everyone at school...

337
00:17:30,340 --> 00:17:34,480
Never mind that. Right now, you should be
thinking about the haiku for the contest.

338
00:17:34,880 --> 00:17:35,900
Grandpa...

339
00:17:36,780 --> 00:17:40,960
Grandpa only cares about haiku.
He doesn't care about how I feel.

340
00:17:41,980 --> 00:17:44,420
He tells everyone to go on the Narrow Road,

341
00:17:44,840 --> 00:17:46,380
but why can't I go?

342
00:17:47,000 --> 00:17:49,520
Matsuo, do you actually hate haiku?

343
00:17:49,520 --> 00:17:50,160
No.

344
00:17:52,180 --> 00:17:53,680
I like haiku because it's interesting.

345
00:17:53,680 --> 00:17:55,460
I see, it's difficult

346
00:17:55,880 --> 00:17:57,640
I don't really like umeboshi either, though.

347
00:17:57,640 --> 00:17:59,740
But Grandpa says they're
good for your body, so...

348
00:18:00,260 --> 00:18:02,540
You don't have to force yourself.
Eat these instead.

349
00:18:02,540 --> 00:18:03,560
Yeah, thanks.

350
00:18:04,040 --> 00:18:06,100
But I'll eat the umeboshi first,
then I'll eat those too.

351
00:18:06,100 --> 00:18:09,100
I see. Alright, there's plenty, so eat up.

352
00:18:10,960 --> 00:18:12,880
I'm starving, so I think I can eat them.

353
00:18:12,880 --> 00:18:14,320
Alright, let's eat.

354
00:18:15,260 --> 00:18:16,220
Yes, but

355
00:18:16,220 --> 00:18:17,800
Thank you very much.

356
00:18:18,280 --> 00:18:21,480
Senpai, it doesn't look like
we've reached Honda-san yet.

357
00:18:21,480 --> 00:18:23,420
I wonder if Grandpa plans to keep waiting.

358
00:18:24,940 --> 00:18:25,740
Nana-chan,

359
00:18:25,740 --> 00:18:27,800
Has Honda-san come here?

360
00:18:27,800 --> 00:18:28,880
Actually,

361
00:18:28,880 --> 00:18:30,780
Welcome, Reiko-san!

362
00:18:31,620 --> 00:18:32,440
You see,

363
00:18:34,260 --> 00:18:35,200
The Narrow Road to the Deep North

364
00:18:35,800 --> 00:18:36,160
That's right.

365
00:18:36,160 --> 00:18:39,280
At his age,
he's gone and lured a child away!

366
00:18:40,960 --> 00:18:49,500
A police officer luring a child away? Honda-san understands people's feelings.
He's the kindest person I know. I believe in Honda-san.

367
00:18:49,920 --> 00:18:57,100
I heard Honda-kun had a fight with his girlfriend and got dumped,
but it seems Honda-san was just worrying for nothing.

368
00:18:59,760 --> 00:19:01,420
Answering the phone, Honda.

369
00:19:01,420 --> 00:19:03,040
Hello, senpai.

370
00:19:03,040 --> 00:19:07,480
Honda, you idiot,
where the hell are you now?

371
00:19:07,480 --> 00:19:09,180
We're in Nikko today.

372
00:19:09,180 --> 00:19:11,480
The weather's great and it feels wonderful.

373
00:19:11,480 --> 00:19:13,340
Nikko? You idiot!

374
00:19:13,340 --> 00:19:14,360
Listen, Honda.

375
00:19:15,240 --> 00:19:18,220
What? I can't hear you well, senpai.

376
00:19:18,220 --> 00:19:19,660
Listen carefully, damn it.

377
00:19:20,940 --> 00:19:22,340
I'm angry, so hurry up.

378
00:19:22,340 --> 00:19:23,280
Shut up!

379
00:19:24,540 --> 00:19:25,800
Just get going already!

380
00:19:25,800 --> 00:19:27,120
Yes, understood.

381
00:19:27,120 --> 00:19:28,560
I'm going right now.

382
00:19:29,580 --> 00:19:33,620
It cut off!
Honda, I wasn't talking to you just now!

383
00:19:34,260 --> 00:19:37,960
Because the customer's phone is
somewhere out of signal range.

384
00:19:37,960 --> 00:19:39,220
Whoa! Ixa!

385
00:19:39,920 --> 00:19:43,340
"Kasane" must be the name
of the double pink carnation.

386
00:19:43,340 --> 00:19:44,100
There!

387
00:19:49,400 --> 00:19:50,260
Honda!

388
00:19:50,400 --> 00:19:52,440
What's up, Matsuo boy?

389
00:19:52,440 --> 00:19:54,620
N-nothing. I just called out to you.

390
00:19:54,620 --> 00:19:56,160
Heh, just called out

391
00:19:57,380 --> 00:19:59,360
We're friends, right? You and me.

392
00:19:59,360 --> 00:20:00,400
What was that?

393
00:20:01,440 --> 00:20:02,680
Nothing.

394
00:20:04,020 --> 00:20:06,620
It's the phone.
Hang on, I'm pausing this for a sec.

395
00:20:06,620 --> 00:20:07,300
Yeah.

396
00:20:13,180 --> 00:20:14,340
Honda-san

397
00:20:17,080 --> 00:20:18,040
Who is it from?

398
00:20:18,040 --> 00:20:21,780
No, I was finally trying to forget about it.

399
00:20:21,780 --> 00:20:24,480
Hello, Honda-san, where are you right now?

400
00:20:24,480 --> 00:20:25,180
Hello?

401
00:20:26,580 --> 00:20:29,320
Hello, Honda-kun is crying,
so I took the phone.

402
00:20:29,320 --> 00:20:33,040
You're Kyūichi-kun, right?
Please, tell Honda-san

403
00:20:33,040 --> 00:20:34,700
that he has something he wants you to see.

404
00:20:35,200 --> 00:20:36,300
Something to see?

405
00:20:36,400 --> 00:20:38,500
Who are you talking to? Give me that.

406
00:20:38,500 --> 00:20:40,520
Is that Kyūichi? Kyū, Kyū-chan?

407
00:20:44,780 --> 00:20:46,180
Hello? Nana?

408
00:20:46,180 --> 00:20:49,660
Hello, yeah, who is this? Honda-san?

409
00:20:49,660 --> 00:20:51,160
Well...

410
00:20:51,160 --> 00:20:53,200
If it's Honda-san, please put him on.

411
00:20:53,200 --> 00:20:55,300
Bring the boy back home right away.

412
00:20:56,160 --> 00:21:01,000
You must come back. Matsuo-kun has a lot on his mind,
so please listen to what he has to say.

413
00:21:01,500 --> 00:21:06,540
It's Honda-san, isn't it? Matsuo-kun's grandfather
wants to speak with him. Please give him back.

414
00:21:07,440 --> 00:21:08,960
Hello, Honda-chan!

415
00:21:10,880 --> 00:21:18,280
Honda-san, what happened? The call dropped?
What, it got cut off? Grandpa was really worried.

416
00:21:18,760 --> 00:21:20,740
Nana-chan, he said there's
something he wants you to see.

417
00:21:20,840 --> 00:21:21,800
Something to see?

418
00:21:22,020 --> 00:21:22,740
That's what he said.

419
00:21:22,880 --> 00:21:24,200
Grandpa says to come home.

420
00:21:24,780 --> 00:21:26,400
You're the one who wants to go home, right?

421
00:21:26,500 --> 00:21:27,620
Not really, for me.

422
00:21:28,040 --> 00:21:29,440
It's fine, I don't mind going back.

423
00:21:29,960 --> 00:21:32,460
But let's finish this trip
together someday, okay?

424
00:21:32,780 --> 00:21:33,140
Yeah.

425
00:21:38,060 --> 00:21:38,940
It flew off!

426
00:21:41,380 --> 00:21:42,380
W-where is it?

427
00:21:42,880 --> 00:21:43,560
Over there

428
00:21:48,280 --> 00:22:08,380
Uuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuu

429
00:22:08,380 --> 00:22:09,160
Grandpa!

430
00:22:09,340 --> 00:22:11,500
Were you hurt? Are you hungry?

431
00:22:11,620 --> 00:22:12,860
Grandpa, I'm sorry.

432
00:22:12,980 --> 00:22:14,860
It's all right, it's all right.
Come on, let's go inside.

433
00:22:17,280 --> 00:22:19,100
No-no-jaan!

434
00:22:19,540 --> 00:22:20,900
It's making me cry.

435
00:22:21,360 --> 00:22:22,600
What's wrong, Reiko?

436
00:22:23,040 --> 00:22:26,720
Nada-chan's manga this time
is more moving than ever.

437
00:22:26,940 --> 00:22:28,420
It really tugs at your heartstrings.

438
00:22:28,620 --> 00:22:30,280
Let me read the next one.

439
00:22:30,520 --> 00:22:31,280
Me too, me too.

440
00:22:31,380 --> 00:22:32,860
If you like, here, take this.

441
00:22:33,580 --> 00:22:34,400
Honda-kun!

442
00:22:34,580 --> 00:22:35,620
Yoi-shoo, yoi-shoo.

443
00:22:36,040 --> 00:22:37,940
They're all the same magazine, aren't they?

444
00:22:38,380 --> 00:22:39,920
Whenever I see one, I end up buying it.

445
00:22:40,400 --> 00:22:42,860
Honda, you made up with your girlfriend,
didn't you?

446
00:22:42,860 --> 00:22:43,820
Well, yeah.

447
00:22:43,820 --> 00:22:46,360
Thanks to you, Honda.

448
00:22:47,200 --> 00:22:50,300
I've gained the confidence to keep
working hard as a priestess of love.

449
00:22:50,660 --> 00:22:53,420
You'll keep watching over me from now on,
won't you?

450
00:22:53,420 --> 00:22:55,840
I'm always watching you, Nada-chan.

451
00:22:55,840 --> 00:22:57,360
Because I'll keep watching over you.

452
00:22:57,960 --> 00:22:58,320
Thank you.

453
00:22:58,800 --> 00:23:01,880
Nada-chan, you two seem even
more lovey-dovey than before.

454
00:23:02,600 --> 00:23:05,780
Honda and the others are probably
more interesting than the manga.

455
00:23:05,780 --> 00:23:07,560
Honda...

456
00:23:08,460 --> 00:23:10,680
So you really talked things
through with your grandpa.

457
00:23:10,680 --> 00:23:14,200
Yeah, so we decided to do soccer too,
not just haiku.

458
00:23:14,200 --> 00:23:15,640
The match is next week.

459
00:23:15,640 --> 00:23:18,160
I'm really going to cheer
you on with Nada-chan.

460
00:23:18,560 --> 00:23:19,840
So you made up.

461
00:23:21,400 --> 00:23:22,360
Well, see you later.

462
00:23:22,360 --> 00:23:25,340
Yeah, that's great, Matsuo-kun.

463
00:23:26,480 --> 00:23:28,320
By the way, where's Senpai today?

464
00:23:28,320 --> 00:23:29,880
That's the thing, they haven't shown up.

465
00:23:29,880 --> 00:23:32,240
Apparently they haven't
returned to the dorm either.

466
00:23:32,240 --> 00:23:34,080
I wonder where they went.

467
00:23:36,740 --> 00:23:39,500
Gathering the summer rains, swift

468
00:23:39,500 --> 00:23:41,860
Where on earth is this place?

469
00:23:41,860 --> 00:23:44,140
Someone tell me.

470
00:23:45,040 --> 00:23:45,980
the Mogami River.

471
00:23:52,460 --> 00:23:55,360
It's like someone is calling out,

472
00:23:55,980 --> 00:23:57,700
after the rain has stopped.

473
00:23:59,200 --> 00:24:01,960
I walked while looking back.

474
00:24:01,960 --> 00:24:04,540
Led along by the hand of a gacha.

475
00:24:05,640 --> 00:24:11,720
That strange feeling I had back then.

476
00:24:12,960 --> 00:24:16,980
So on the tiles of the arcade street,

477
00:24:16,980 --> 00:24:22,780
I tried walking only on the black ones.

478
00:24:25,280 --> 00:24:28,920
Everyone was a child once,

479
00:24:28,920 --> 00:24:30,880
but they've all forgotten.

480
00:24:32,020 --> 00:24:38,360
Politicians with their self-important faces,
and aunties with blue eyeshadow.

481
00:24:38,850 --> 00:24:43,940
Try turning that corner, won't you?

482
00:24:45,000 --> 00:24:49,140
You can meet everyone, everyone.

483
00:24:51,240 --> 00:24:57,560
There's Kame-ari surely there's Kame-ari.

484
00:24:58,540 --> 00:25:02,300
Come on over, everyone, to our town.

485
00:25:02,300 --> 00:25:06,980
There's Kame-ari,

486
00:25:08,260 --> 00:25:10,260
surely Kame-ari.

487
00:25:11,480 --> 00:25:15,540
Come on over, everyone, to our town.

488
00:25:16,440 --> 00:25:17,000
Thank you.

489
00:25:19,460 --> 00:25:22,440
Someone who inspects
the police box is coming?

490
00:25:22,580 --> 00:25:24,600
That's the kind of news
that'd fire up the Chief.

491
00:25:24,600 --> 00:25:25,500
Hey, Chief.

492
00:25:25,500 --> 00:25:28,180
Chief, you've got a terrible fever,
don't you?

493
00:25:28,180 --> 00:25:30,520
Are you okay, staggering around like that?

494
00:25:30,520 --> 00:25:32,100
If the Chief is like this...

495
00:25:32,100 --> 00:25:33,640
What's going to happen to the police box?

496
00:25:33,640 --> 00:25:36,560
Next time, Chief, please just stay in bed.

497
00:25:37,140 --> 00:25:37,880
Take care, then.

498
00:25:38,620 --> 00:25:40,860
That place is Kameari.

499
00:25:41,860 --> 00:25:44,500
Well, I'm sure it's Kameari.

500
00:25:45,440 --> 00:25:49,200
Everyone, come on over to our town!

501
00:25:50,300 --> 00:25:50,780
Thank you.

